Every so often we like to have a bit of fun with what Tessera can do. This week's Fun Friday feature is postcards!

The Tessera Postcard generator lets you select any 10km × 6km patch of land on Earth and renders it straight from the model's embeddings. You can also render the same location in a range of colour palettes, revealing the depth of information hidden in the embeddings.

Below are a few more postcards from our archive, minus the location labels this time. Have a guess before you reveal the answers.

<figure class="mystery">
  <img src="/blog/postcard-jantar-mantar.webp" alt="A false-colour Tessera postcard of a city with wide radial avenues meeting at roundabouts, rendered in oranges, teals and purples, with a river winding down the right-hand side" loading="lazy" />
  <details class="spoiler">
    <summary>Reveal location</summary>
    <p>Jantar Mantar, New Delhi, India</p>
  </details>
</figure>

<figure class="mystery">
  <img src="/blog/postcard-noordoostpolder.webp" alt="A false-colour Tessera postcard of a landscape of rectangular fields in a strict grid, rendered in reds, purples and blues, with a densely detailed town at the right" loading="lazy" />
  <details class="spoiler">
    <summary>Reveal location</summary>
    <p>Noordoostpolder, Netherlands</p>
  </details>
</figure>

<figure class="mystery">
  <img src="/blog/postcard-victoria-falls.webp" alt="A false-colour Tessera postcard of a river cutting through a zig-zag gorge, rendered in greens and blues with a vivid magenta plume at the top" loading="lazy" />
  <details class="spoiler">
    <summary>Reveal location</summary>
    <p>Victoria Falls, Zambia–Zimbabwe</p>
  </details>
</figure>

Fancy making one yourself? Head to the [postcard generator](https://tee.cl.cam.ac.uk/postcard.html), pick a spot that means something to you — home, a favourite holiday spot, wherever — and send someone a postcard of how Tessera sees it.

The Tessera Postcard generator is a feature of the [Tessera Embeddings Explorer](https://tee.cl.cam.ac.uk/), our browser-based tool for interactively exploring, labelling, and building lightweight classifiers on Tessera embeddings, no coding required.

